R = {
"domotex": dict(
 esig=[("Floors laid as installed.","Areas of the stand with your product actually laid, with skirtings, thresholds, transitions and changes of material, so visitors see how the floor behaves in a real room."),
  ("Walls for large formats.","Book-style, sliding or wall displays for slabs, planks and large samples, with structures sized on the weight and easy to leaf through."),
  ("Grazing light.","Low, side lighting that brings out grain, relief, brushing and finishes, plus neutral light to compare colours without colour casts."),
  ("Tables for architects and fitters.","Loose samples to take away, data sheets, catalogues and a quiet table to talk about specifications, quantities and delivery times."),
  ("Winter build-up.","Transport and laying in January, with tight timings, short days and weather margins: materials leave Italy already checked, with spares for replacements.")],
 tempi="DOMOTEX is in January: laying floors at the fair needs crews and materials ready in time, so design should close in autumn, with quantities and formats to lay defined by November. Stand production falls in December, with transport right after the holidays. We update the official 2027 dates as soon as they are out.",
 qa=[("Can you lay our flooring in the stand?","Yes, we coordinate the laying with your fitters or our partners during build-up: we prepare the subfloor, calculate quantities with a safety margin and allow the time adhesives and finishes need."),
  ("Do you make displays for slabs and planks?","Yes, made to measure: book-style, sliding or wall-mounted, sized on formats and weights. We design them to be reused at other fairs and in your showroom."),
  ("Do you also build at Cersaie?","Yes, we build stands at Cersaie in Bologna: if you exhibit at both fairs you can reuse displays and part of the structures.")]),
"imm-cologne": dict(
 esig=[("Complete settings.","Living rooms, bedrooms and kitchens with walls, floors and ceilings like a showroom, with doors, mock windows and details that make the room feel real."),
  ("High-end finishes.","Lacquers, woods, fabrics and metals chosen with samples approved before production, because visitors touch everything and notice every joint."),
  ("Designed lighting.","Accent and diffused light calibrated on the materials, with colour temperatures chosen to show wood, fabric and lacquered surfaces at their best."),
  ("Order area.","A lounge for retailers, with catalogues, price lists and fabric and finish samples, where orders and area exclusivity deals are closed."),
  ("Transport from Italy in January.","Stand and furniture coordinated on the same loading days, right after the holidays, with packaging that protects finished pieces during travel and build.")],
 tempi="imm cologne is in mid-January: the stand is produced between November and December, so design should close in autumn, together with the choice of pieces and finishes to show. If you also exhibit at the Salone del Mobile, we can design elements that serve both fairs and keep them in our warehouse between editions.",
 qa=[("Can the imm cologne stand be reused at the Salone del Mobile?","Partly, yes: we design modular walls and furniture that adapt to different sizes and store them between fairs. Graphics and finishes change at each edition, the structure stays."),
  ("Do you handle transport and build in Cologne?","Yes, with an Italian contact person: production in Italy, transport, build at Koelnmesse, support during the fair and dismantling, with the paperwork for the organiser handled by us."),
  ("Do you also build at the Salone del Mobile?","Yes, we build stands at the Salone del Mobile in Milan, a few kilometres from our offices, and at the other furniture fairs in Italy.")]),
"boot-dusseldorf": dict(
 esig=[("Boarding gangways and steps.","Safe structures to go on board, with handrails, non-slip treads and comfortable slopes, sized on freeboard height and a constant flow of visitors."),
  ("Platforms around hulls.","Decks that hide the cradles and create a pontoon around the boat, finished in wood or synthetic teak like a real quay."),
  ("Sales offices and lounges.","Lounges and desks for negotiations, financing and configurations, set apart from the aisle but with the boat always in view."),
  ("Technical showcases.","Walls and counters for engines, electronics, components and accessories, with focused light and screens showing installation and operation."),
  ("Nine days of fair.","Sturdy materials that withstand nine days of visitors, storage for catalogues and stock, and technical support throughout the show.")],
 tempi="boot is at the end of January: stand production falls in December and transport right after the holidays. It is best to close the design by October, coordinating it with boat transport and with the vehicle entry slots that Messe Düsseldorf assigns well in advance.",
 qa=[("Do you build gangways to board the yachts on show?","Yes, made to measure on freeboard height, with steps, handrails and platforms around the hull. We design them once we have the boat and cradle dimensions."),
  ("Do you also build at the Genoa Boat Show and METSTRADE?","Yes: the Salone Nautico in Genoa and METSTRADE in Amsterdam. Gangways and furniture can serve several shows."),
  ("Do you organise transport from Italy?","Yes for the stand; boats travel with specialised carriers and we coordinate timings at the fair, so hulls and stand go in in the right order.")]),
"gruene-woche": dict(
 esig=[("Sales and tasting counters.","Washable tops, tills and showcases to sell and offer tastings all day, with sinks and a prep area hidden from the public."),
  ("Refrigeration and services.","Fridges, refrigerated displays and electrical power sized for ten days of continuous work, with switchboards and sockets exactly where needed."),
  ("Regional pavilions.","Stations for several producers under one regional identity, each with its own name, sign and counter but shared graphics and materials."),
  ("Generous storage.","A closed, accessible back room to restock every day, with shelving for boxes and space for goods delivered during the fair."),
  ("Hard-wearing materials.","Floors, counters and graphics designed for a constant crowd of families and visitors, easy to clean in the evening and tidy every morning.")],
 tempi="Grüne Woche is in mid-January: for regional pavilions it is best to start in summer, when producer sign-ups are collected and stations are defined. Production falls in December and transport to Berlin in the first days of the year, so graphics and exhibitor lists should close by November.",
 qa=[("Do you build regional pavilions with many producers?","Yes, we design the shared area and stations and handle graphics and build with one contact person. Each producer receives practical instructions to set up their own counter."),
  ("Do you supply fridges and sales counters?","Yes, for hire together with the stand, with certified electrics and power calculated on the number of fridges and appliances you will use."),
  ("Do you also work at Fruit Logistica in Berlin?","Yes, we build stands for Fruit Logistica, held at Messe Berlin a few weeks after Grüne Woche.")]),
"biofach": dict(
 esig=[("A truly sustainable stand.","Reusable wood, honeycomb cardboard, recyclable fabrics and plants: materials consistent with organic values, also chosen so they can be rebuilt or recycled after the fair."),
  ("Tastings.","A washable counter, fridge and hidden prep area, to offer oil, cheese, pasta or wine without clutter in front of buyers."),
  ("Organic-shop shelving.","Shelves that recreate the specialist store, so buyers immediately see formats, packs and how they would look on their own shelf."),
  ("Italian group stands.","Stations for several companies under a shared identity, with a common area for meetings and tastings and graphics that make the origin clear."),
  ("Certifications on show.","Organic labels, supply chain and origin readable from afar, because at BIOFACH buyers look first for guarantees and traceability.")],
 tempi="BIOFACH is in mid-February: design by November, production in December and January and transport to Nuremberg in early February. A wooden stand you own, kept in our warehouse, can be reused at Sana Food, Cibus or other fairs, and it is the most sustainable choice in terms of cost too.",
 qa=[("Can the stand be reused for several fairs?","Yes, we design it modular and store it ourselves: it is more sustainable and costs less each edition. Graphics and layout change, the wooden structure stays."),
  ("Do you build regional group stands at BIOFACH?","Yes, with coordinated stations, shared graphics and one contact person, who also handles relations with the organiser and each exhibitor's deadlines."),
  ("Do you also build at Sana Food?","Yes, in Bologna we build stands for Sana Food, the Italian fair for organic and natural products.")]),
"embedded-world": dict(
 esig=[("Connected demo stations.","Counters with power, wired network and screens for every demo, sized on the boards and devices you bring to the fair."),
  ("Tidy cabling.","Hidden but accessible trunking and service spaces, so a demo can be fixed without dismantling the counter and with no cables in the aisle."),
  ("LED walls and screens.","Videos and interfaces visible from the aisle, to explain in a few seconds what a tiny component does."),
  ("Technical meeting rooms.","Private spaces for meetings on projects and specifications, where engineers and customers can discuss products not yet announced."),
  ("Clean look.","Light materials, even lighting and essential graphics: in a hall full of screens, an orderly stand stands out and makes demos easier to read.")],
 tempi="embedded world is in mid-March: design by December, with the list of demos and the power they need, so connections are requested from NürnbergMesse in time. For a small stand or a first participation, modular solutions ready in a few weeks are enough.",
 qa=[("Can you provide network and power for many demos?","Yes, we design stations around the demos you bring and request power and connections from the organiser. During build-up we test every point before opening."),
  ("Do you supply screens and LED walls?","Yes, for hire, installed and connected by our crews together with the stand lighting."),
  ("Do you also build at electronica and productronica?","Yes: electronica and productronica in Munich, which alternate in even and odd years.")]),
"internorga": dict(
 esig=[("Working machines.","Electrical power, water and drains calculated on the equipment, because ovens, dishwashers and coffee machines must really work in front of visitors."),
  ("Demo kitchens and counters.","Islands for show cooking, bars and tastings, with heat- and stain-resistant tops and room for both cooks and spectators."),
  ("Furniture for venues.","Settings of bars, restaurants and breakfast rooms, showing furniture, tableware and equipment where they will be used."),
  ("Technical back area.","Space for washing, stock and spare parts, hidden from visitors but handy for those working at demos all day."),
  ("Welcoming distributors.","Tables and lounges for business meetings with importers, hotel chains and restaurant groups.")],
 tempi="Internorga is in spring: services must be requested early from Hamburg Messe, so the design should close by December, with the list of machines and their data sheets. We update the official 2027 dates as soon as they are out.",
 qa=[("Do you bring water and drains into the stand?","Yes, we design them and coordinate them with the fair's technical services, from drain positions to raised floors to route the pipes."),
  ("Do you also build at HostMilano?","Yes, we build stands at HostMilano with working machines: if you exhibit at both fairs you can reuse kitchens and counters."),
  ("Does the stand travel from Italy to Hamburg?","Yes: production in Italy, transport and build with an Italian contact person, who remains your contact during the fair and dismantling.")]),
"logimat": dict(
 esig=[("Floors for moving systems.","Level, load-bearing floors for robots, shuttles and trucks, with no steps or joints that could disturb guides or sensors."),
  ("Protected demo areas.","Barriers and safe paths around demonstrations, so visitors can watch closely without entering the working zone."),
  ("Racking on show.","Tall structures built to Messe Stuttgart rules, with stability calculations and documents delivered on time."),
  ("Software on show.","Screens and stations showing WMS, controls and warehouse flows, connected to the systems working on the stand."),
  ("Meeting room.","A closed space for warehouse projects and negotiations, where layouts, capacities and delivery times are discussed calmly.")],
 tempi="LogiMAT is in mid-March: for stands with working systems the design must close by December, when weights, footprints and power of each machine are needed. For small exhibitors, modular stands are enough and quick to prepare even at the start of the year.",
 qa=[("Can the stand floor take robots and trucks?","Yes, we provide level, load-bearing floors suited to the vehicles you bring. We need weights, wheels and paths to choose the right floor."),
  ("Can you build tall racking in the stand?","Yes, within the heights and calculations required by Messe Stuttgart, which we submit with the stand design."),
  ("Do you also build at transport logistic?","Yes, we also work at transport logistic in Munich, the major logistics fair held in odd years.")]),
"fibo": dict(
 esig=[("Floors for equipment.","Load-bearing platforms and sports flooring that carry heavy machines, absorb dropped weights and survive four days of testing."),
  ("Try-out areas.","Free space around each machine, so trainers and gym owners can really try it without blocking the aisle."),
  ("Stage and audio.","For workouts and presentations, with sound and lights sized on the space and within the volume limits set by the fair."),
  ("Premium gym look.","Brand lights, materials and graphics that make the stand feel like a top-level gym, with mirrors and careful finishes."),
  ("Distributor area.","A lounge for negotiations with gym chains, hotels and importers, away from the noise of the try-outs.")],
 tempi="FIBO is in April: the design should close by January, together with the choice of machines and their weights, needed to size the platforms. If you also exhibit at RiminiWellness, we can design one stand for both fairs and keep it in our warehouse.",
 qa=[("Can platforms take heavy gym equipment?","Yes, we size them on real weights and choose suitable sports flooring, impact-resistant in free-weight areas."),
  ("Do you build stages for workouts and presentations?","Yes, made to measure, with audio and lights for hire. We also include storage for instructors' changes and equipment."),
  ("Do you also build at RiminiWellness?","Yes, we build stands for RiminiWellness: if you exhibit at both you can reuse platforms, walls and furniture.")]),
"ligna": dict(
 esig=[("Platforms for heavy machines.","Loads calculated on the machine data sheets and floor channels for electrics, compressed air and extraction."),
  ("Extraction and air.","Space and connections for extraction and compressed-air systems, designed with your technicians and coordinated with Deutsche Messe's services."),
  ("Guarding.","Distances and barriers for demonstrations, so visitors watch the machining closely, safely and according to fair rules."),
  ("Wooden stand.","Walls and furniture that show machining quality: at LIGNA the stand itself can become a sample of what your machines do."),
  ("Double-deck stand.","Meeting rooms above the machines, away from the noise, overlooking the demo area, with structural documents for the organiser.")],
 tempi="LIGNA is in May in odd years: for stands with working machines you start the summer before, because weights, connections and delivery plans are agreed with the fair months before build-up. If you also exhibit at Xylexpo, we can design elements reusable at both fairs.",
 qa=[("Can you build the stand with wood machined by our machines?","Yes, we design elements that show what your machines do and integrate them into the stand: walls, counters or machined details become part of the demo."),
  ("Do you build double-deck stands in Hanover?","Yes, with structural calculations and documents for Deutsche Messe, prepared by qualified engineers and delivered by the deadlines."),
  ("Do you also build at Xylexpo?","Yes, we also work at Xylexpo in Milan, the Italian woodworking machinery fair.")]),
"transport-logistic": dict(
 esig=[("Meeting rooms.","Closed or semi-closed spaces for back-to-back meetings with forwarders, shippers and ports, bookable throughout the fair."),
  ("Bar and welcome.","A counter that makes visitors stop, with coffee and light catering, often where unplanned meetings begin."),
  ("Screens and LED walls.","For maps, networks, routes and terminal videos, readable from afar in Messe München's large halls."),
  ("Group stands for ports and regions.","Stations for several operators under one identity, with a shared hospitality area and each partner's name and logo clearly visible."),
  ("Double-deck stand.","For large operators, meeting rooms upstairs and welcome downstairs, with structural calculations and paperwork for the fair.")],
 tempi="transport logistic is at the end of April in odd years: for large or group stands it is best to start the previous autumn, when partners sign up and sizes and stations are fixed. The 2027 dates are official, so planning can start now.",
 qa=[("Do you build group stands for ports and inland terminals?","Yes: shared area, stations for each operator and one contact person for the organising body. We also collect each partner's logos and texts."),
  ("Can you build a double-deck stand in Munich?","Yes, with calculations and documents for Messe München, prepared by qualified engineers and delivered by the fair's deadlines."),
  ("Do you also build at LogiMAT and Transpotec?","Yes: LogiMAT in Stuttgart and Transpotec in Milan, for companies attending several logistics fairs in the same year.")]),
"achema": dict(
 esig=[("Load-bearing platforms.","For skids, pumps, tanks and plants, with loads calculated on data sheets and floor channels for cables and piping."),
  ("Cutaways and details.","Plinths and lights showing the inside of components, because technical visitors want to see seals, materials and machining."),
  ("Technical walls.","For valves, instruments and panels, with sturdy fixings and a layout that follows the process from raw material to product."),
  ("Meeting rooms.","For projects, specifications and quotes, with screens for drawings and process diagrams and a quiet setting for negotiations."),
  ("Handling.","Lifting equipment and timings coordinated with the fair, so heavy components go in before walls and furniture.")],
 tempi="ACHEMA is in mid-June 2027 and takes place every three years: for large stands it is best to start in autumn 2026, together with the list of equipment to show. Space is allocated well in advance and Messe Frankfurt's technical deadlines come months before opening.",
 qa=[("Can platforms take heavy plants and skids?","Yes, with loads calculated on data sheets and documented for Messe Frankfurt. We also provide routes to connect demo plants."),
  ("Can you build a double-deck stand at ACHEMA?","Yes, with structural calculations and paperwork for the fair, prepared by qualified engineers."),
  ("Do you organise transport from Italy?","Yes for the stand; machinery travels with your forwarder and we coordinate timings so it reaches the fair in the right order.")]),
"automatica": dict(
 esig=[("Safe robot cells.","Fences, barriers and distances that meet your engineers' requirements and fair rules, with transparent panels to show the robot at work."),
  ("Platforms and plinths.","For robots and machines, with cable routes, anchoring where needed and level surfaces that do not vibrate during fast moves."),
  ("Power and network.","For robots, vision systems and connected software, with dedicated switchboards and stable wired connections for the whole fair."),
  ("Screens and demos.","Interfaces and videos visible from the aisle, explaining cycle times, precision and applications even to passers-by."),
  ("Meeting rooms.","For integrators and engineering departments, where automation projects are discussed with drawings, quotes and confidential data.")],
 tempi="automatica is at the end of June 2027: for working robot cells the design must close by March, with footprints, weights and safety zones defined with your engineers. If you also exhibit at Laser World of Photonics, we coordinate both stands on the same days at Messe München.",
 qa=[("Can you build robot cells with guarding?","Yes, we design structure and guarding according to your engineers' instructions and the fair rules, with access for maintenance and part changes."),
  ("Do you supply screens and LED walls?","Yes, for hire, with certified electrics and hidden cabling, installed and connected by our crews."),
  ("Do you also build at SPS Italia and MECSPE?","Yes: SPS Italia in Parma and MECSPE in Bologna, the main Italian fairs for automation and mechanical engineering.")]),
"laser-world-of-photonics": dict(
 esig=[("Shielded zones.","Cabins or blackout walls for working lasers, following the fair's safety rules and your laser safety officer's instructions."),
  ("Stable benches.","Rigid, level tops for optics and instruments that do not pass on vibrations from the floor and passing visitors."),
  ("Controlled light.","Dimmable lighting that does not disturb demos, with darker zones where contrast and precision are needed."),
  ("Showcases for components.","Protected display of optics, sources and delicate devices, with built-in lights and locks where value requires."),
  ("Technical rooms.","Spaces for meetings with researchers and engineers, with screens for data and drawings, away from hall noise.")],
 tempi="Laser World of Photonics is at the end of June 2027: shielded zones must be designed with your engineers and approved by the fair, so it is best to start in winter. Production and transport close in May, leaving room for any changes requested by Messe München.",
 qa=[("Can you build shielded cabins for working lasers?","Yes, we design them with your safety officers and submit them to Messe München, with doors, viewing windows and signage required by the rules."),
  ("Do you also work at automatica on the same days?","Yes, we can coordinate two stands at once, with shared crews and logistics: see automatica."),
  ("Do you handle transport and build in Munich?","Yes, with an Italian contact person and build crews coordinated by us, from material delivery to dismantling.")]),
}
